      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} This does help in editor to stop the erratic snapping. In game, the object simply locks itself to the constrained object without any snapping (in my testing I took the previous example and simply placed the target on my head and enabled local space). The object would simply follow my head as if I had constrained it normally. It seems there is an inconsistency between in editor and in game?",
